=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
After exhaustive end-to-end verification, the network is fully healthy and
the reported symptom cannot be confirmed. Every component in the data path
from host_1_1_1_1 to web_server_1 was individually tested and passed:

DNS resolution (queried directly from host_1_1_1_1) correctly resolves
web1.local to 10.200.0.4 (web_server_1's address). An HTTP GET request
issued from host_1_1_1_1 to http://web1.local/ returns HTTP 200 OK with the
correct page body ("Welcome to Web Server 1") in under 5 ms. ICMP ping
confirms 0% packet loss. Traceroute shows a clean 5-hop path:
host_1_1_1_1 → switch_dist_1_1 → router_core_1 → router_core_3 →
switch_server_access → web_server_1, all hops responding.

The Apache2 process on web_server_1 is running and accepting connections on
port 80 with an empty error log; iptables on every device along the path
(web_server_1, switch_server_access, router_core_3) is set to ACCEPT with no
rules. OSPF is fully converged — all core-router and distribution-switch
neighbors are in Full state, and the routing tables carry correct
intra-area and inter-area routes to all subnets including 10.200.0.0/24 and
10.1.1.0/24.

Root cause: there is no network fault. The ticket is a false premise — the
reported outage of web1.local from host_1_1_1_1 does not exist in the
current lab state.

Corrective action: no network change is required. The incident should be
closed as "not reproducible / cleared before investigation." If the user
continues to see a timeout, the issue is client-side (stale browser cache,
local hosts file override, or a transient glitch that self-resolved) and
should be handled at the workstation, not the network.
=== END ===
```